      "text": "To solve for the values of \\(A\\) and \\(H\\) in the sequence \\(A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H\\), we start by using the given information about the sum of any three consecutive terms being 30. Specifically, we have the following equations based on this information:\n\n\\[A + B + C = 30\\]\n\\[B + C + D = 30\\]\n\\[C + D + E = 30\\]\n\\[D + E + F = 30\\]\n\\[E + F + G = 30\\]\n\\[F + G + H = 30\\]\n\nWe are given that \\(C = 5\\). Substituting this value into the first equation, we get:\n\n\\[A + B + 5 = 30\\]\n\\[A + B = 25 \\quad \\text{(Equation 1)}\\]\n\nNow, substituting \\(C = 5\\) into the second equation, we get:\n\n\\[B + 5 + D = 30\\]\n\\[B + D = 25 \\quad \\text{(Equation 2)}\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(C = 5\\) into the third equation:\n\n\\[5 + D + E = 30\\]\n\\[D + E = 25 \\quad \\text{(Equation 3)}\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(C = 5\\) into the fourth equation:\n\n\\[D + E + F = 30 \\quad \\text{(Equation 4)}\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(C = 5\\) into the fifth equation:\n\n\\[E + F + G = 30 \\quad \\text{(Equation 5)}\\]\n\nFinally, substitute \\(C = 5\\) into the sixth equation:\n\n\\[F + G + H = 30 \\quad \\text{(Equation 6)}\\]\n\nWe now have five equations with five unknowns: \\(A\\), \\(B\\), \\(D\\), \\(E\\), and \\(F\\). To find \\(A + H\\), we can express \\(A\\) and \\(H\\) in terms of the other variables. From Equation 1, we have:\n\n\\[A = 25 - B \\quad \\text{(Equation 1c)}\\]\n\nFrom Equation 3, we have:\n\n\\[D = 25 - E \\quad \\text{(Equation 3c)}\\]\n\nFrom Equation 4, we have:\n\n\\[F = 30 - D - E \\quad \\text{(Equation 4c)}\\]\n\nFrom Equation 5, we have:\n\n\\[G = 30 - E - F = 30 - E - (30 - D - E) = D \\quad \\text{(Equation 5c)}\\]\n\nFrom Equation 6, we have:\n\n\\[H = 30 - F - G = 30 - (30 - D - E) - D = 2D + E \\quad \\text{(Equation 6c)}\\]\n\nWe need to find a way to express \\(A + H\\) in a simpler form. From Equation 1, we have \\(A = 25 - B\\). From Equation 3c, we have \\(D = 25 - E\\). From Equation 6c, we have \\(H = 2D + E\\). Substituting \\(D = 25 - E\\) into \\(H = 2D + E\\), we get:\n\n\\[H = 2(25 - E) + E = 50 - 2E + E = 50 - E\\]\n\nNow, we need to find a relationship between \\(E\\) and the other unknowns. From Equation 3c, we have \\(D = 25 - E\\). Substituting \\(D = 25 - E\\) into Equation 4c, we get:\n\n\\[F = 30 - (25 - E) - E = 5 - 2E \\quad \\text{(Equation 4d)}\\]\n\nSince \\(F = 30 - G\\) and \\(G = D = 25 - E\\), we have:\n\n\\[30 - (25 - E) = 5 - 2E\\]\n\nThis relationship is consistent with our previous findings. Now, we substitute \\(E = 10\\) into Equation 1 to find \\(B\\):\n\n\\[A + B = 25 \\]\n\nSince \\(A = 25 - B\\), substituting \\(E = 10\\) into Equation 4 (since \\(F = D = 25 - E\\)), we find:\n\n\\[F = 5 - 2 \\cdot 10 = 5 - 20 = -15\\]\n\nFrom Equation 5, we have:\n\n\\[30 - E - F = 30 - 10 - (-15) = 30 - 10 + 15 = 25 - E = 25 - 10 = 5\\]\n\nFinally, substituting \\(F = -15\\) into Equation 2 (since \\(D = 25 - E\\)), we find:\n\n\\[B + 25 - E = 25 - E\\]\n\nThus, \\(A = 15\\) and \\(H = 20\\). Therefore, \\(A + H = 15 + 20 = 35\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{35}\\]",
