      "text": "We are given the sequence $A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H$ with $C=5$ and the sum of any three consecutive terms is 30.\nWe know that $A+B+C=30$, $B+C+D=30$, $C+D+E=30$, $D+E+F=30$, $E+F+G=30$, and $F+G+H=30$.\nWe can use this information to set up a system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n& A+B+5=30,\\\\\n& B+C+5=30,\\\\\n& C+D+5=30,\\\\\n& D+E+5=30,\\\\\n& E+F+5=30,\\\\\n& F+G+5=30,\\\\\n& G+H+5=30,\\\\\n& A+B+C+D+E+F+G+H=30\n\\end{align*}\nSimplifying these equations, we get\n\\begin{align*}\n& A=25-B,\\\\\n& C=15-B,\\\\\n& D=15-C=40-B,\\\\\n& E=15-D=25-B,\\\\\n& F=15-E=9-B,\\\\\n& G=15-F=18-B,\\\\\n& H=15-G=27-B,\\\\\n& A+B+C+D+E+F+G+H=30\n\\end{align*}\nWe can now add all these equations together:\n$$\n(25-B)+B+(40-B)+(25-B)+(9-B)+(18-B)+(27-B)+(A+B+C+D+E+F+G+H)=300.\n$$\nSimplifying, we get\n$$\n130-5B+3(A+B+C+D+E+F+G+H)=300.\n$$\nSince we know that $A+B+C+D+E+F+G+H=30$, we can substitute this into the equation:\n$$\n130-5B+3(30)=300.\n$$\nSimplifying, we get\n$$\n130-5B+90=300.\n$$\nFinally, we can solve for $B$ to find that $B=1$.  Then $A=24$ and $H=12$, so $A+H=36$.  Therefore, the answer is $\\boxed{36}$. The answer is: 36",
